<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Lifecycle Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Products can lose momentum when teams fail to adapt their strategy
                    as the product moves through different lifecycle stages. Effective
                    lifecycle management helps organizations identify challenges early
                    and respond with the appropriate product strategy.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Changing Customer Needs:</b> Continuously collect customer feedback and monitor behavior to keep the product relevant.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Unclear Product Direction:</b> Maintain a clear product vision, roadmap, and measurable objectives.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Slow Product Development:</b> Improve prioritization, collaboration, delivery processes, and technical capabilities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Declining Product Adoption:</b> Improve onboarding, usability, customer education, engagement, and feature discovery.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Increasing Competition:</b> Monitor market changes and continuously improve product differentiation and value.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Legacy Technology:</b> Plan technical modernization, scalability improvements, security updates, and technical debt reduction.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Product Decline:</b> Evaluate declining performance and determine whether optimization, repositioning, replacement, or retirement is appropriate.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

