                <p>
                    Product retirement is an important part of lifecycle management when
                    a product no longer provides sufficient value or when a better
                    replacement solution becomes available. A structured transition
                    approach helps protect customers and business operations.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Analyze product performance, customer usage, maintenance costs, and strategic relevance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Determine whether optimization, modernization, replacement, or retirement is the appropriate path.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Develop migration and transition plans for existing customers.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Communicate retirement timelines and available alternatives clearly to customers and stakeholders.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
